 -- Kernora Developers <developers@kernora.invalid>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:00:00 -0700

kernora-desktop (1.4.30) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Reduce motion no longer breaks the shell. With animations off Kirigami
    reports a 1 ms long duration, so M3.motionScale was 0.005 rather than 0:
    the springs behind the quick settings shade, switches and the volume OSD
    ran with a 2 ms response and diverged. The shade then stayed an invisible
    full-screen window that swallowed every click. motionScale is now 0 at
    1 ms or less, springs pick a stable step for any stiffness and stop on
    non-finite values, and live wallpapers treat 1 ms as reduced motion.
  * A widget's toolbar closes when the pointer leaves the widget and its
    toolbar, and whenever edit mode ends. Plasma 6.3 does not reset an item's
    edit mode when the layout leaves edit mode, so a toolbar opened before a
    settings dialog or a move to another window could stay up.
  * The weather widget scales its reading to the room inside its shape. The
    cloud shape for overcast skies is a fifth shorter than the others, so
    the text overflowed it and the widget looked squashed.
  * Live wallpapers pause only for maximised or full-screen windows on their
    own screen. The task model's exact screen match failed with mixed
    scaling; each window's centre is now tested against the screen instead.
  * Album art in the media widget and the quick settings card is retried
    when a download fails, instead of staying on the placeholder.
  * System monitor widgets follow theme changes. Their sensor colours are
    generated from the accent once and stored; a diverted applet main.qml
    recolours the generated ones when the accent changes and keeps colours
    picked by hand.
  * Restart is in the launcher next to Shut Down, and the shut down dialog
    offers Restart too.
  * htop, now part of the base system, gets a Kernora app icon.
  * The lock screen shows the wallpaper set for it instead of always drawing
    Shapes over it; Kernora Shapes stays the default through
    /usr/share/kernora/xdg, added to XDG_CONFIG_DIRS. The login screen shows
    the wallpaper an administrator last chose: kernora-greeter-background,
    run through polkit without a password for members of sudo, records it in
    the theme's theme.conf.user and copies a picture to
    /var/lib/kernora/greeter.

