kernora-desktop (1.4) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Install the Material 3 components as QML modules for the Kernora
    applications: org.kernora.m3 (tokens, text, icons, sliders, state
    layers) and org.kernora.ui (list rows, groups, pages, dialogs, fields,
    search, navigation, snackbars).
  * Light variants of the Plasma theme and the window decoration, so light
    or dark switches the whole system; both palettes in the QML tokens.
  * Material text is drawn with Qt's own rendering: native rendering
    spaced glyphs unevenly under Material's letter spacing.
  * App icons for the Kernora applications, the Terminal and the
    installer, drawn like the Settings icon; new Material Symbols for the
    applications.
  * Terminal: Alacritty under the Kernora name, with light and dark colours
    from the design tokens, as the desktop's terminal; its window is titled
    after the prompt ("user@host: ~") rather than "Alacritty".
  * KDE's System Settings, Alacritty and Calamares entries are hidden in
    favour of the Kernora ones.
  * Default account picture: the mark on a tonal circle.
  * Kernora login screen for SDDM: Kernora Shapes behind a large clock and
    a Material 3 account card, in English and Russian.
  * Installer: Material 3 steps, buttons and pages (welcome, location,
    keyboard, account, summary, finish), a slideshow over Kernora Shapes,
    and the kernora-installer launcher, which starts Calamares with the
    Kernora look in the session's language.
  * Installer keyboard: a Material 3 keyboard that shows what every key
    types in the chosen layout and variant (from XKB, by
    tools/gen-keyboard-maps) and lights up while typing; layout, variant,
    model and switch as dropdown fields, named in the installer's language
    (xkeyboard-config's translations), also on the summary.
  * Installer: cities sorted by their translated names; Russian for the
    messages Calamares leaves untranslated (tools/gen-qm); the live
    language service is removed from the installed system.
  * Installer partition page in Material 3 with Kernora's Calamares: option
    cards, partition list and dialogs styled by the branding's stylesheet.qss
    (tools/gen-installer-style), Material Symbols for its icons
    (tools/gen-installer-icons); kernora-calamares depends on calamares
    (>= 3.3.14-1kernora1).
  * Push buttons without icons (ShowIconsOnPushButtons=false), as Material
    buttons carry text only.
  * Kernora lock screen: Kernora Shapes behind a large clock, the account
    card with its password pill and the power actions, as on the login
    screen. It replaces Plasma's (diverted) and unlocks through the same
    kscreenlocker authenticator.
  * Kernora on-screen display: volume and brightness as a thick Material 3
    slider with the icon riding on the fill, messages as a pill; replaces
    Plasma's (diverted).
  * Kernora power menu for log out, restart and shut down: large Material 3
    tiles on a card, the automatic action counting down.
  * Alt+Tab shows Kernora window cards (a KWin window switcher): the app's
    icon and title over a rounded thumbnail, the chosen card ringed.
  * The web browser is LibreWolf, in the Kernora colours: a generated light
    and dark theme (tools/gen-browser-theme) that LibreWolf installs into
    new profiles as a distribution add-on, made the default by kernora.js
    in /usr/share/librewolf/browser/defaults/preferences (read after the
    browser's own defaults), which also has files picked in Kernora's
    chooser through the desktop portal. LibreWolf's own policies (uBlock
    Origin, no telemetry) are left as they are.
  * /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list: LibreWolf opens web pages and PDFs, Photos
    pictures, the Text Editor JSON and XML (LibreWolf claims those too).
  * Kernora notifications: popups laid out like Android's (the app's
    badge, "App · time", title, text, the picture beside it, tonal action
    buttons, M3 progress for file jobs) and a history of connected cards
    with Do not disturb and "Clear all"; the panel bell badges unread
    notifications and rings with the jobs' progress. Plasma's applet keeps
    its C++ plugin; its QML entry point is diverted.
  * Notification job details show how much is copied again (Plasma's
    QML failed on an undeclared variable).
  * Quick settings: Android's media card for whatever plays (any MPRIS
    player) -- the artwork behind a scrim, a play button that squares off
    while playing, and a seek bar that flows as a wave.
  * Quick settings: a Dark Theme tile, which switches the whole system the
