  * Kernora boot menu (tools/gen-grub-theme): the mark over the entries as
    rounded Material cards, the chosen one on the secondary container, in
    Roboto (GRUB fonts made at build time with grub-mkfont, Cyrillic
    included). The ISO carries it, and grub.d/kernora.cfg sets it with the
    graphical terminal for an installed system.
  * Styles: Material Design 1, 2 and 3. tools/kernora_design.py defines all
    three generations from the one seed, and the QML tokens carry them all,
    following ~/.config/kernorarc at run time:
    - their palettes: grey paper with a vivid accent; white and #121212;
      tonal;
    - their corners per kind of component, and their shadows;
    - their buttons: capitals and raised in the older two, pills in
      Material 3;
    - their switches, sliders and quick settings: Lollipop's bare icons,
      Android 9's round toggles, Material 3's tiles.
    The colour schemes, Plasma theme, Kvantum and window frames are
    generated for each (KernoraMD2Dark, kernora-md2, ...). The shell, the
    Qt Quick style and the shared components follow, with Material 3's own
    expressive details kept.
  * Kernora clipboard (org.kernora.clipboard): Meta+V opens the clipboard
    history as a Material 3 sheet above the panel, with search, text,
    links, pictures and files as connected cards, "Remove" and "Clear
    all". It loads Plasma's Klipper, which nothing in the panel started
    before; Klipper's own popup leaves Meta+V to it (a kglobalshortcutsrc
    for new accounts), and the history keeps pictures (/etc/xdg/klipperrc).
  * The sheet's second tab is emoji, as on a phone keyboard: Meta+. opens
    it (Plasma's emoji selector's shortcut file is diverted), with
    category tabs, recently used ones, search by English and Russian names
    and keywords, and Noto Color Emoji. The emoji and their names are
    generated from Unicode's and CLDR's data (tools/gen-emoji-data).
  * A USB drive or memory card plugged in brings a notification from Files
    ("USB drive connected", with "Open"), which mounts it and opens it in
    Files; Kernora's panel has no device notifier to pop up instead
    (quick settings' DeviceSource.qml on Plasma's device model,
    kernora-devices.notifyrc).
  * Plasma theme: the focus and hover rings of fields and buttons sit on the
    control (Plasma lays them out by their margins, which drew KRunner's
    focus ring 16px around its field), and pill fields and buttons are half
    as round as they are tall, so no seam runs through their middle.
  * Material Symbols for the OSD's switches (Wi-Fi, touchpad, on-screen
    keyboard, mobile data, sleep blocked), for the display switch (Meta+P:
    one screen, the other, mirrored, extended left or right), and for
    reply, send and clear; links as Material's link symbol.
  * Login screen without SDDM's on-screen keyboard, which covered the
    account card.
  * New panels and launchers pin Files and Settings instead of KDE's
    System Settings.
  * The settings window of the desktop and of every applet in Kernora's
    layout: sections as a navigation list, the current one on a rounded
    pane under its headline, Material buttons. The desktop's pages are
    Material groups -- wallpaper and desktop kind as choices, the folder
    view's Location, Icons and Filter, Mouse Actions with a dialog that
    catches the new click, an applet's shortcut, and About. Plasma's files
    are diverted; what they save is unchanged. Buttons at the end of a
    list row take their own clicks (they went to the row). Plasma's
    picture and slideshow pages get room for their grid of pictures.
  * Material Symbols: create_new_folder for folder-new.
  * Live wallpapers of Material shapes at play, next to Kernora Shapes and
    in its flat Material 3 tones: Tower (a stack of shapes rocks, tumbles
    down and hops back together, simulated on the shapes' outlines),
    Rhythm (a ring of shapes in a pendulum wave -- spirals, stars and back
    to a circle -- over a blob that morphs with it) and Marble Run (shape
    marbles roll down ramps, ring the posts and ride a lift back up); each
    with a tonal palette from gen-wallpaper-assets, which also gives the
    shapes' convex hulls. Picture
    wallpapers are gone: Kernora Ember is removed and Breeze's picture is
    kept out by a dpkg path-exclude.
  * Kernora cursors (kernora_cursors, tools/gen-cursor-theme): Material
    glyphs with ember badges; wait and progress animate Material 3
    Expressive's morphing loading indicator. Xcursor and KWin's scalable
    SVGs; the default in Plasma, SDDM and x-cursor-theme.
  * No bouncing icon while programs start (/etc/xdg/klaunchrc): the busy
    cursor is the only launch feedback.
  * org.kernora.ui: StyleCard removed; the style is chosen from a list.

